-- Layer: our usage: what building hyperactivity uses now, no claim of the paper behind it (the four layers: see the language-implementation-remainder node of task-graph/hyperactivity.cub).
-- lib/document.cub — a document of the repository as an object of the code (2026-11-13). The
-- surface form `document "path"` (src/syntax.c, p_atom) reads the file when the declaration is read,
-- relative to the file being read as import's paths are, and fails if there is no such file, so a
-- reference to a document that does not exist does not check. It elaborates to `document-at path
-- digest`, digest the SHA-256 of the file's bytes in hex: a definition that mentions a document has a
-- content key that changes exactly when the document's content does. What a document is for is said
-- where it is referred to (for the task graph: its essential context, lib/task-graph.cub).
import "core.cub"
data Document = document-at (path : List Word) (sha256 : List Word)
